@startuml
title ai-qa — aiqa run <env> (Q1)

actor Owner
participant "CLI" as CLI
participant "RunScenarios" as UC
participant "BrowserSession\n(Playwright, saved Access state)" as BS
participant "DescriptorSource\n(hub dashboard API)" as DS
participant "ScenarioSource\n(GitHub raw @commit)" as SS
participant "AgentRunner\n(claude -p + Playwright MCP)" as AG
participant "VerdictGate / Redactor" as VG
database "runs/<id>/ (files)" as FS

Owner -> CLI: aiqa run feat-x [--tag smoke]
CLI -> UC: execute(env, filters)
UC -> FS: create run dir, run.json state=CREATED (atomic write)
UC -> BS: preflight(dashboard URL) with saved state
alt no state / lands on Access login
  UC -> FS: state=REFUSED reason=login_required
  UC --> CLI: exit 3 "run aiqa login"
end
UC -> DS: get(env) through the browser session
alt unknown / not READY / not allHealthy
  UC -> FS: state=REFUSED reason=environment_not_ready
  UC --> CLI: exit 3 (no agent call)
end
UC -> SS: load(repo, commit) for each service
UC -> BS: preflight(entryUrl) -> storage state with the env-host cookie (temp file 0600)
UC -> FS: state=RUNNING, scenarios listed (PENDING), commits fixed
loop each scenario (sequential), while run budget remains
  UC -> AG: run(prompt(K3), mcp_config(allowed origins, storage state path,\noutput dir = scenario dir), caps) in an empty temp cwd
  note right: process group; wall-clock timeout;\nstream transcript to scenario dir
  AG --> UC: AgentOutput(result text, transcript, turns, seconds, exit)
  UC -> VG: accept(output, transcript, files, caps)
  VG --> UC: ScenarioResult (PASSED/FAILED/SKIPPED + reason)
  UC -> VG: redact-scan scenario dir (cookie/JWT patterns)
  UC -> FS: write scenarios/<id>/result.json, update run.json (atomic)
end
UC -> FS: write report.json (qa-report/v1, schema-validated), summary.md; state=COMPLETED
UC -> FS: delete temp storage state
UC --> CLI: exit 0 if no FAILED else 1
@enduml

@startuml
title ai-qa — aiqa login (Q1)

actor Owner
participant "CLI" as CLI
participant "BrowserSession (headed Playwright)" as BS
participant "Cloudflare Access + GitHub SSO" as CF

Owner -> CLI: aiqa login
CLI -> BS: open dashboard URL in a headed window
BS -> CF: redirect to Access login
Owner -> CF: signs in (GitHub SSO / PIN) — typed by the owner only
CF --> BS: session cookies (HttpOnly)
BS -> CLI: landed on the dashboard origin
CLI -> CLI: verify the Access cookie is HttpOnly; save storage state\n~/.config/aiqa/access-state.json (0600); print only "session saved"
@enduml
